    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Iudex">Iudex</ref> 15.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>Hyt ys awriten: ‘Ne onfoh ðu nænigne had on dome; né ne ara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.a"/> ðú for nanum, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þu þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> riht ne deme’.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>Scriptum est: Non attendas personam hominis in iudicio, nec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.12"/> pro aliquo facies<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.13"/>, ut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.c"/> a uero denies<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.14"/> et iniuste iudices!</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>Es steht geschrieben: ‘Nicht begünstige du irgend eine Person im Urtheilspruch und um Keines willen schone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Iudex_15-1.lnote.de.1"/> unterlassend, den richtigen Spruch zu ertheilen’.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It is written: ‘Do not favour any person in judgment, and for no one's sake be lenient so as to fail to give the right judgment’.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-g-a">It is written: “Don’t look (over-)favourably upon any individual, nor give honour to any (in such a way) that justice is not served.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Deuteronomy 16:19 (cf. Exodus 23:2–3)</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="476">Deut. 16, 19</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Deut. 16, 19</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="editorial">U: translator unrecorded: check</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">476</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so R;</hi> ne <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus R; ne the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">476</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">facis <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">facis <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">476</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus Exod.</hi> 23, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from Exod. 23, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">476</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">declines <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">declines <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Iudex_15-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">476</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">non misereberis pauperis in iudicio (<hi rend="italic">aus Exod.</hi> 23, 3) <hi rend="italic">Isidor</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">non misereberis pauperis in iudicio (from Exod. 23, 3) Isidor</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Iudex_15-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">269</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verf. weicht frei ab von Isidors Exodus-Zitat; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. 4²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The author departs freely from Isidor’s quotation from Exodus; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 4²</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
